      "id": 32233,
      "name": "Exosat",
      "slug": "exosat",
      "former_names": [],
      "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/4ada0c6c689e415dd6275bd653f7e5171ef2d584.png",
      "website": "https://www.exosat.com",
      "all_locations": "Singapore, Singapore",
      "long_description": "Exosat is building a sovereign alternative to Starlink by mass manufacturing thousands of satellites that work as cell towers in space. By designing our architecture with zero U.S-origin parts and manufacturing with overseas partners, our satellites can be built at under a tenth of the usual cost and launched from any nation to bypass bottlenecks in launch capacity.\r\n\r\nWe're starting off by selling connectivity to OEMs and network operators, but will eventually use the distributed compute across our satellite constellation to support sovereign AI use cases as well.\r\n\r\nWe've already signed $400M+ in LOIs to work with operators across Central Asia, Southeast Asia, and the Middle East, booked our first satellite launch next year, and hold an 11,000 satellite filing with the ITU to build the largest comms network outside of the U.S. and China.",
      "one_liner": "Building a sovereign Starlink",
      "team_size": 1,
      "highlight_black": false,
